WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.336
A significant new boost for Ukraine's
fight against Russia.

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.638
First reported here on CNN.

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:09.109
The United Kingdom sending Long-Range
Cruise missiles to Ukraine

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.013
just ahead of Kyiv's expected
counteroffensive against Russia.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:15.382
Our Brian Todd is digging
deeper on the impact

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:18.118
this potentially could have out there
on the battlefield.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:19.352
Brian, what are you learning?

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.154
Wolf, we've learned that these new British
missiles

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:25.225
can strike deep into the heart
of Russian held territory in Ukraine.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:28.395
But they were only delivered
after the Ukrainians made an important

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:31.097
promise to the British government.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.200
A senior U.S.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.605
military official tells CNN it's a game
changer for Ukraine on the battlefield.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.174
The storm shadow cruise missile.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.411
CNN chief national security correspondent
Jim Sciutto reports.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:48.448
Great Britain has now delivered
multiple storm shadow missiles to Ukraine.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.551
A weapon
that has the capability to strike deep

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:54.120
into Russian held territory
in eastern Ukraine.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:58.024
Jim Sciutto cites a Western official
as saying Britain has received

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:01.861
assurances from the Ukrainian government
that the missiles will only be used

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.498
within Ukrainian sovereign territory,
not inside Russia.

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.967
It's notable that U.K.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:11.037
officials have said repeatedly
they view Crimea

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:14.874
as sovereign Ukrainian territory
illegally annexed by Russia.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.710
So this leaves open the possibility,
at least, that Ukrainian forces

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.314
can use this not only to attack
Russian forces in eastern Ukraine,

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:26.252
but also in Crimea, which Russia views
as strategically important

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:30.590
as this video from the manufacture
and BDA missile systems shows,

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:34.627
the storm shadow is launched
from the air flies low to the ground,

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:37.864
and its range is what will make
the difference for the Ukrainians.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.701
155 miles, about triple
the range of the missiles

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.370
the Ukrainians have
that were provided by the U.S..

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:46.106
What part

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:49.542
of Russia's forces can Ukraine degrade
with the new storm shadow?

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:50.343
It's going to allow them

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:54.047
to strike much deeper
and to go after especially fixed targets,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:02:00.687
whether it be ammunition depots or runways
or any kind of big installation

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:03.890
that the Russians
have been able to operate with impunity.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.826
The storm shadow doesn't complete
Ukraine's wish list.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:09.496
The Ukrainians have long
been asking the U.S.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:13.700
to provide the long range surface
to surface army tactical missile systems,

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:18.571
called by their acronym attack ships
that have a range of 185 miles.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:19.772
But analysts say

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:23.510
the Storm Shadow has capabilities
that the attack system doesn't have.

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:28.681
Those capabilities include a GPS
snap of the Earth navigation capability.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:33.052
And the reason for that,
it actually allows for more efficient

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.122
use of firepower
and more effective targeting

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.024
Now, this

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.860
isn't the first time that Britain has gone
further than the U.S.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:44.564
in providing Ukraine with advanced
weaponry and sometimes doing it sooner.

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:49.135
Britain was the first ally to commit to
sending modern Western tanks to Ukraine.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.804
The challenge to tanks before the U.S.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.941
announced it would send the M1
Abrams tanks Wolf.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.510
Brian Todd reporting for us.
Thank you very much.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.479
Joining us now is Matthew Schmitt,
an associate

00:02:59.479 --> 00:03:02.515
professor of national security
and political science at the University

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.284
of New Haven in Connecticut.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.351
It's good to see you.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.120
Good to see you, John.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.388
Okay, so here is the U.K.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:12.525
defense minister, Ben Wallace, announcing
in parliament that Britain will do what

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:16.563
the US has so far been unwilling to do,
and that's provide long range missiles

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:21.501
Storm
Shadow is a long range, conventional,

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.836
only precision strike capability.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.973
It complements
the long range systems already gifted,

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:31.377
including high models and harpoon
missiles, as well as Ukraine's own Neptune

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:34.714
cruise missile and longer range
missions elsewhere gifted.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.484
The donation of these weapon systems
gives Ukraine the best chance

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.521
to defend themselves
against Russia's continued brutality.

00:03:43.923 --> 00:03:45.291
So these are stealth missiles

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.061
or stealthy missiles which are fired
from the air by a fighter jet.

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:49.262
And the manufacturer says

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:53.132
they have the ability to deliver precision
effects from a safe stand of distance

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.836
against high value targets
such as well-protected control bunkers

00:03:57.003 --> 00:04:00.473
and centers, key infrastructures
and military installations.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.244
So how would you see these missiles
being used during the counteroffensive?

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:09.616
The first thing that they're going to do
is attack Russian artillery.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:14.053
That's the number one way that the Russian
military has been killing Ukrainians.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:17.757
And they will try to denude
that capability as much as they can.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.927
The second thing that they'll do is attack
supply routes,

00:04:21.628 --> 00:04:23.863
particularly ammo and fuel.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:26.899
And then I wouldn't be surprised
if they have enough.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:28.034
That's the key here, right?

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:31.971
How many is Britain giving them
and how fast to restock

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.041
the Kurds bridge or something
like that of high symbolic value?

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:38.344
And it seems the UK is sending
what is a shorter range variant.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:41.414
155 miles as opposed to 350 miles.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:46.552
But even at 135 miles, these missiles,
which have been used effectively in Syria,

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:51.224
Iran and Libya, have a capability
to strike deep into Russia.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.158
I mean, if you get the borderline

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:56.162
you go 150 miles north of there
and you're deep inside Russian territory.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:05:00.033
Now Western official told CNN
that the UK has received assurances

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:01.968
from the Ukrainian government
that these missiles

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:06.272
will be used only within Ukrainian
sovereign territory and not inside Russia.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:09.442
UK officials have made frequent
public statements identifying Crimea

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:12.912
as Ukrainian sovereign territory,
describing it as illegally annexed.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:17.850
So what happens, though, if the Ukrainians
decide not to be held to that?

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:21.020
Some of it is some dramatic changing event
and they decide

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.489
they need to fire these missiles
well deep into Russian territory.

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:24.257
What happens then?

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:28.428
Well, I think if there's some
dramatic event that changes the conditions

00:05:28.428 --> 00:05:30.930
on the battlefield and changes
the political conditions

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.366
then all bets are off.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:37.136
But short of something like that,
I think Ukrainians are going to

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:40.907
are going to very much
stay within the parameters that the U.S.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.842
and that the U.K. have set for them.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.977
They know where the where
the money's coming from.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:47.480
They know where the weapons are coming
from, and they're not going to risk it.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.349
And if you look what the U.S.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:52.752
has been unwilling to supply the talks,
they only go a short

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:56.255
distance
further than the Britain missiles do.

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.291
So they don't have a lot of differences
between these two.

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.094
So does this mean that the United States
may be more inclined

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:02.695
to provide these longer range missiles?

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:04.430
That's a

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.032
pattern that we've seen throughout the war

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.900
where the Biden administration
has said no.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.770
And then three, four or six weeks
later, has said yes

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:12.972
and sort of inch deeper
and deeper into the war.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:16.142
So I wouldn't be surprised
if that's what happens here.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:19.145
And that, in fact,
may be part of the political calculation,

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:23.082
which is that if the UK sort of breaks
the barrier on this,

00:06:23.316 --> 00:06:24.484
then it's easier for the U.S.

00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:25.918
to come along and say, well,

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.221
it doesn't matter
now, does it, because Britain did it.

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.022
So we might as well

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:33.059
And Britain was the first to supply
Ukraine modern better.

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:33.793
Thanks.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:35.461
Now, the first of the long range missiles

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.597
and from the very beginning
has been pushing the U.S.

00:06:37.597 --> 00:06:39.098
and the other allies to a lot more.

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.968
Is that mostly driven
by this long list of covert attacks on UK

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:45.671
soil by the Russians
the poisoning Sergei Skripal in 2018

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:48.975
and Alexander
actually was poisoned back in 2006.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:52.245
Now I think it's part of the signaling

00:06:52.245 --> 00:06:56.215
to Russia that they need to back off
on these attacks in the U.K.

00:06:56.215 --> 00:07:00.720
I think a lot of it is just old school
pride and a lot of it's just revenge.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:05.525
And you know whatever is remaining
of motivation I think is that the U.K.

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.260
is trying to punch above its weight again

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:10.463
right is trying to get back in there
and say we are one of the leading

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.567
forces of foreign policy in the world
and this is the way that they can do it.

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:17.336
Yeah. And it's been effective so far,
I guess.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.438
Matthew, thanks for being with us.

00:07:18.438 --> 00:07:19.472
We appreciate it.

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:20.706
My pleasure.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:24.777
We're getting word of new Russian strikes
in two regions of Ukraine.

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:28.281
Officials say Russian artillery
and air force unleashed a barrage

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:31.284
of attacks on her son region, killing
at least one person.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:34.220
Four others were wounded over the past
24 hours,

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:37.056
while separate attacks on the city
of Slovyansk.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:42.228
About 600 kilometers to the northeast left
one person dead and 12 others injured.

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:43.529
Meanwhile, Ukraine

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:47.200
is reportedly working to smooth the way
for its upcoming counter-offensive.

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:50.736
Two senior Western officials
say Kiev has already started what's called

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:54.173
shaping operations
for its expected attack, which means it's

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:57.510
launching selective strikes
to soften Russian defenses.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.613
For more, Scott
McClain joins us from London.

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:05.051
So, Scott, what more are we learning about
this so-called shaping operation

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:08.087
and the counteroffensive
that will presumably follow?

00:08:08.921 --> 00:08:12.692
Yeah, so the question is whether or not
the counteroffensive has begun at all.

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:15.595
And for the answer,
it really depends on who you ask.

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:18.931
If you ask President Zelensky,
he says that the Ukrainians need

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:22.735
a bit more time to get more Western
weapons, more Western equipment

00:08:22.735 --> 00:08:26.239
into the country before they can
really begin that counteroffensive.

00:08:26.272 --> 00:08:27.840
But if you ask the head of the volunteer

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.377
private military contractor
on the Russian side, Yevgeny Prigozhin,

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:34.280
he says that Zelensky is lying
and that the counteroffensive

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.381
is already in full swing.

00:08:35.381 --> 00:08:38.584
And he points to the situation in Baku
where even he concedes that

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:41.387
the Ukrainians have had some success
as of late.

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:44.657
The actual
Ukrainian military says that, yes,

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:48.694
it has been able to exploit some Russian
weaknesses on the flanks of this city,

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:52.532
particularly the northern
and southern parts of the city

00:08:52.532 --> 00:08:56.903
where there is dynamic fighting,
in their words, going on at the moment.

00:08:56.903 --> 00:08:59.405
And they say that
while they are definitely on offense,

00:08:59.405 --> 00:09:01.374
they're not calling it a counter
offensive.

00:09:01.374 --> 00:09:05.745
The deputy defense minister has said
just today that the Ukrainians

00:09:05.745 --> 00:09:10.583
have managed to advance two kilometers
on the Russians in just the past week.

00:09:10.616 --> 00:09:11.984
And as a result,

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:16.322
the Russians actually last night
had to put out a pretty unusual late

00:09:16.322 --> 00:09:20.393
night statement denying reports
that the Ukrainians had made a major

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:24.830
breakthrough in the region, saying
that the situation there is under control.

00:09:24.864 --> 00:09:28.834
Of course, the big risk for the Russians
is that the Ukrainians may be able

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:33.072
to push forward on those outer flanks
there and actually surround the Russians,

00:09:33.072 --> 00:09:37.243
either pushing them,
forcing them to retreat or perhaps

00:09:37.476 --> 00:09:40.112
forcing them to surrender
after what has been eight

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:43.316
months
and months of bloody fighting there.

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:47.253
And as you mentioned, Kim
senior Western officials are saying that

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:50.856
what Ukraine is doing at the moment
is something called shaping, which means

00:09:51.023 --> 00:09:55.161
using airstrikes to take out things
like artillery systems, take up things

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:56.996
like command centers and weapons

00:09:56.996 --> 00:10:01.067
depots, things like that,
in order to sort of shape the battlefield,

00:10:01.067 --> 00:10:05.271
to make it easier for advancing troops
to actually move on the ground.

00:10:05.304 --> 00:10:08.341
This could go on for several days
before we see anything

00:10:08.608 --> 00:10:11.544
sort of resembling a full scale
counteroffensive.

00:10:11.544 --> 00:10:14.847
And this is something
that we also saw ahead of the Ukrainian

00:10:14.847 --> 00:10:18.951
counteroffensive in Harrison last summer,
which resulted in the Ukrainians

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:21.854
taking back
a very wide swath of territory again.

00:10:22.321 --> 00:10:22.655
All right.

00:10:22.655 --> 00:10:24.991
Thanks so much for the update.
Scott McClellan appreciate it.

